From 3333333333333333333333333333333333333333 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Phillip Abbott <phillipa@vivi.io>
Date: Thu, 10 Jul 2026 14:30:00 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] androidmedia: force JNI codec backend (disable NDK AMediaCodec)

Interim fix, pending upstream report.

On GStreamer 1.26 the NDK AMediaCodec backend (preferred when
media/NdkMediaCodec.h is present) breaks pacing for non-live HTTP playback
on Android 9: every frame is QoS-dropped as late, back-pressure never
engages, and decode races to EOS in seconds with only the first frame or
two rendered (the preroll). The JNI backend -
the only backend in our 1.20 build - paces correctly. A/B (pkg 252 NDK vs
254 JNI) confirmed on Android 9 (goldfinger and Clevertouch); not seen on
other versions. Codec selection is unchanged; only how the codec is
operated differs. See "Moonraker GStreamer Upgrade" decision record, D2.

Upstream supports building without NdkMediaCodec.h, so JNI-only is a
supported configuration. Drop once fixed upstream.
---
 subprojects/gst-plugins-bad/sys/androidmedia/meson.build | 10 +-
 1 file changed

diff --git a/subprojects/gst-plugins-bad/sys/androidmedia/meson.build b/subprojects/gst-plugins-bad/sys/androidmedia/meson.build
index 1111111111..2222222222 100644
--- a/subprojects/gst-plugins-bad/sys/androidmedia/meson.build
+++ b/subprojects/gst-plugins-bad/sys/androidmedia/meson.build
@@ -83,7 +83,15 @@
 # Build an Ndk support if its headers exists. We don't actually link into it
 # but use only type definations (and then rely on dlopen and dlsym), so this
 # doesn't affect compatibility with older Android versions.
-if cc.check_header('media/NdkMediaCodec.h')
+#
+# Vivi (interim fix, pending upstream): disable the NDK AMediaCodec backend
+# so gstamc uses the JNI backend, as our 1.20 build did. On Android 9 the
+# NDK backend defeats back-pressure on non-live HTTP playback (frames
+# QoS-dropped as late, decode races to EOS, only the first frame or two
+# rendered); A/B-confirmed on goldfinger and Clevertouch. Codec selection
+# is unchanged. See "Moonraker GStreamer Upgrade" decision record, D2.
+# Revert to a bare cc.check_header(...) once fixed upstream.
+if false and cc.check_header('media/NdkMediaCodec.h')
   androidmedia_sources += ndk_sources
   extra_cargs += [ '-DHAVE_NDKMEDIA' ]
   extra_deps += [ cc.find_library('android', required : true) ]
